{
  "name": "malformed",
  "integration": "forescout-counteract",
  "description": "Every documented shape is violated somewhere on the legacy path: the field index carries a bare string and an unnamed entry, the host index carries a string element, a null hostId, a blank hostId, and a duplicate row, and the property documents come back as a list, as a host with a string fields member, and as a 404. Every bad record must be skipped and the run must still import the three real hosts.\n\nHost 4004 carries only placeholder names (UNKNOWN, a bare IP) in its NBT/DHCP properties; it must import on its address with no hostname at all, because a shared placeholder name is a merge hazard. It also pins the date properties against a real deployment shape: a captured property document returns ipv4_report_time as {\"value\": \"true\"} -- a boolean under a date name -- and a deployment rendering that same boolean as \"1\" would parse to epoch 1 and stamp the endpoint 1970-01-01. The unix <= 0 guard does NOT catch that, because unix 1 is above zero, so anything shorter than 10 digits is refused as not-a-date. Neither value may produce a lastSeenTS. POST /api/hosts/discovery answers 404 so the scenario states which path it exercises, and the fallback log line is asserted.",
  "kwargs": {
    "url": "$BASE",
    "username": "webapi-fixture",
    "password": "fixture-password"
  },
  "routes": [
    {
      "name": "login",
      "match": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/api/login"
      },
      "responses": [
        {
          "status": 200,
          "text": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJiYWQifQ.YmFkLXNpZ25hdHVyZS1maXh0dXJl"
        }
      ],
      "when_exhausted": "repeat_last"
    },
    {
      "name": "discovery-not-implemented",
      "match": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/api/hosts/discovery"
      },
      "responses": [
        {
          "status": 404,
          "text": "Not Found"
